From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Anderson <thomasanderson@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:38:57 -0700
Subject: [Ozone] End touch sequences handed off to a drag or move

When a touch sequence is taken over by a drag or window move, the
platform never delivers its release to aura, so aura::Env keeps
reporting a touch as held and the platform's own touch tracking stays
live. WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging uses aura::Env::is_touch_down()
as its liveness check for renderer-initiated touch drags.

X11: X11WholeScreenMoveLoop consumes touch releases while a data drag or
tab-drag window move runs. Record the consumed touch sequences and have
X11Window dispatch a touch cancel for each to its window once the loop
returns. Only sequences that were actually consumed are cancelled, so a
tab drag that re-attaches to a tab strip with the finger still down is
unaffected.

Wayland: the compositor owns touch sequences during a touch-driven data
drag or xdg_toplevel.move and need not send wl_touch.up for them
afterwards (e.g. Weston). Add WaylandEventSource::CancelActiveTouches(),
the touch analogue of ReleasePressedPointerButtons(), and call it when a
data drag session closes and after handing off an interactive move. This
also clears touch_points_, which otherwise kept the touch press serial
valid for drags and caused the next touch with the same id to be
dropped.

Fixed: 574901760
Change-Id: Id5eaaabee30150ccd0bd37316036bf3c6f8ba562
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8612575
Auto-Submit: Thomas Anderson <thomasanderson@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kramer Ge <fangzhoug@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kramer Ge <fangzhoug@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1723297}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): WaylandEventSource::OnTouchCancelEvent on this branch still iterates touch_points_ directly (it predates the upstream id-snapshot/weak-window loop), so CancelActiveTouches() is extracted from that loop body, with the timestamp parameter replacing the local base::TimeTicks::Now(). wayland_data_drag_controller_unittest.cc gains only the TouchDragEndsTouchSequence test (the adjacent upstream RejectReentrantStartSessionDuringWindowDrag test belongs to another change). The X11 and remaining Wayland hunks apply as upstream.

